@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+requires "verification.k"
+
+module SPEC-BODY-MUTATION
+  imports VERIFICATION
+
+  // Body-sensitivity witness: the submitted `total += i` is changed to
+  // `total += 2`. On n = 1 the mutant returns [2], so the real [1] target must
+  // no longer close.
+  claim
+    <k> Call(Name("f"), Int(1)) => ref(0) </k>
+    <env> 0 </env>
+    <scopes>
+      0 |-> scope(
+        "f" |-> closureVal("n", .ParamNames,
+          Assign(Name("result"), ListExpr(.Exprs))
+          Assign(Name("factorial"), Int(1))
+          Assign(Name("total"), Int(0))
+          Assign(Name("i"), Int(1))
+          While(Compare(Name("i"), CmpOp("<=", Name("n"))),
+            AugAssign(Name("factorial"), "*", Name("i"))
+            AugAssign(Name("total"), "+", Int(2))
+            If(Compare(BinOp("%", Name("i"), Int(2)), CmpOp("==", Int(0))),
+              Expr(Call(Attribute(Name("result"), "append"), Name("factorial"))),
+              Expr(Call(Attribute(Name("result"), "append"), Name("total"))))
+            AugAssign(Name("i"), "+", Int(1)))
+          Return(Name("result")), 0),
+        parent(-1))
+      -1 |-> builtinsScope
+    </scopes>
+    <scopeLoc> 1 </scopeLoc>
+    <heap> .Map => 0 |-> list(vCons(1, .ValSeq)) </heap>
+    <heapLoc> 0 => 1 </heapLoc>
+    <stack> .List </stack>
+    <ret> noRet </ret>
+    requires true
+    [label(body-mutant-one)]
+endmodule

codex
The pinning check passed mechanically: parsing both the regenerated module and the three entry-claim closure terms to KORE produced byte-identical program terms, and the helper `#while` matches the submitted `While` constructor exactly. A body mutation inside the claimed closure (`total += 2`) built cleanly and was rejected with the expected final heap `[2]` versus target `[1]`. I’m now auditing all 702 rules and, in particular, the candidate’s `total` predicate and four simplification axioms.
